{"atom_type": "CITATION_OCCURRENCE", "bibkey": "groth2010nano", "content_id": "b003c1fd0ed661190c8e7970c5efff6a5a57384371d56aba5c7997dc868e3386", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "line": 56, "occurrence_id": "b726077b77f91abf23c0d7305e32443a630863e9a1e361a8c7c660554a4c0dd6", "occurrence_index": 0, "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:L56"}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "d8d4f869eebc57bcf73fcab65e2bd067e18f578aab0ae6be8fbe2fe4e230a03b", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "62d81a630ce9e3077a32b988db5f800701a7b527428e4190be2f65a761b7e49f", "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:0", "text": "Agent evaluations increasingly depend on context interventions---retrieval, memory graphs, and prompt contracts---yet published reports often omit null outcomes, parser failures, and negative cells."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "7b54d97bd301237be3d759c3a7019af949607ae1ac3d0b38d987fd7ac4411ab4", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "c5cdf6f3456d7884ff97c3d09a011719133b9d6e06f08e4f396c8eb9e1767696", "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:1", "text": "We present HydraDG, a governed experimental framework that binds substantive model invocations, tool calls, and handoffs to \\emph{Fractal Custody Objects} (FCOs) and a \\emph{Fractal Custody Graph} (FCG)."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "340870fe746d637396c8ecb935119d17baa22b94327196f282018b84b9c871b3", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "dbc1789a08c1b4fe702cbb8500df45df63ebcb2e9acee85aee62b39f60f3cd9e", "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:2", "text": "HydraDG preregisters hypotheses, freezes case manifests and scorers, records raw prompt and response hashes, and preserves terminal states including timeouts, abstentions, and malformed outputs without silent substitution."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "38260336b22929cd3e6aa7b5f260d60fdd0cc2fbc3fd2429bf4c28f7b571665c", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "f11ce19a65456bbb7be5f35903d3ab77769a64477ab7b206cc5a046a27582da7", "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:3", "text": "We report two preregistered studies (EXP-008, EXP-009) comparing flat prose versus structured FCG retrieval for failure-prevention endpoints; both terminate as \\emph{underpowered} under bounded case replication, so confirmatory effect claims are not supported while negative and null evidence remains in custody."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "5493155d2ebd8441309cae289b6961dc25f56607e972ccfbf4b375a65b4d2bdd", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "cadbe7e7c084cac36ac42b4bad7d174676059509c3ebef53cf2a08a3a65bd11c", "parent_occurrence_id": "19f8a394e85892920795d4ba101680e195732489e07277aecb17c4854455c4ff", "source_pointer": "git:cfee4ee7a6a8c418f9c71a37ca96031518d895bc:paper/newinml2026_solo/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:4", "text": "We argue that custody-first evaluation infrastructure supports reproducible agent science rather than optional logging."}
